--- !u!114 &938268073765848576
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 5963329745576076169}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Item Usage System


    Introduced a new three-step item usage flow: select
    an item, choose a target character, and confirm.


    Added cancellation at
    any step of the process.


    Items that do not require a target, such as Skill
    Tree Resets and Restorative Drinks, skip character selection.


    Item usage
    now tracks the source inventory, slot, item, and target character.


    Items
    are removed from their exact source slot, whether they belong to the temporary
    or permanent inventory.


    The usage flow cancels automatically if an item
    changes slots during the process.


    Characters who cannot receive an item
    are shown as unavailable, with an explanation.


    Character-Targeted Items


    Introduced
    a new system for items that apply effects to a specific character.


    Added
    compatibility checks to determine whether an item can be applied to a selected
    character.


    Improved item effect execution to account for the target character''s
    stats.


    New Item: Restorative Drink


    Added Restorative Drinks, which
    heal every character in the playable roster.


    Healing values are configurable
    per item.


    Restorative Drinks do not require a target character.


    Item
    Intensity System


    Introduced a four-level intensity system: +, ++, +++,
    and ++++.


    Item intensity is now represented by symbols instead of directly
    stored numeric values.


    Added a centralized Intensity Library that maps
    stats, modifier types, and intensity symbols to their corresponding values.


    Updated
    the editor interface with a table-based layout for easier balancing.


    Existing
    item assets are migrated automatically to the new format.


    Character Stats
    & Persistence


    Character stat modifications are now saved separately for
    each save slot.


    The current stat value is calculated from the base stat
    plus its saved modification.


    Relative modifiers now apply percentages to
    the current effective stat value.


    Status items are unavailable when no
    save slot is selected, preventing unintended item consumption.


    Improved
    stat retrieval, availability checks, and save operations.


    Deleting a save
    file now affects only the active slot.


    Accuracy System


    Improved the
    combat accuracy system.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
